{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790542549,"nonce":"A8FGbK/j+GY/ecF+fxts5dSDnog=","title":"A fiber's first call does not bind its value to the function's parameter","message":"Stock Wren passes the value of the first call to a fiber whose function takes a parameter; WrenLift passes null, in the interpreter and tiered alike.\n\n    var f = Fiber.new {|start|\n      System.print(\"got %(start)\")\n      var r = Fiber.yield(start)\n      System.print(\"then %(r)\")\n    }\n    System.print(f.call(10))\n    f.call(2)\n\nwren_cli: got 10 / 10 / then 2. wlift --mode interpreter and --mode tiered: got null / null / then 2. Under a wasm AOT build with fibers, the parameter receives the closure itself (the krio body puts the first value at stack[0], which a compiled closure reads as its receiver).","files":null}]}